Mon Nov 16 13:46:13 UTC 2026 - Tina Müller <timueller+perl@suse.de>

- updated to 0.210.0 (0.21)
   see /usr/share/doc/packages/perl-Spreadsheet-XLSX/Changes

  0.21  2026-11-15
      - Decode XML entities and numeric character references once in worksheet
        names before optional character conversion (RT #50705). Support lookup
        by decoded names and report undefined name conversion results.
      - Abort with a clear error when a string converter returns undef
        (RT #84528), while continuing to accept empty converted strings.
      - Decode predefined XML entities and numeric character references once
        in shared and inline strings, including rich text and phonetic hints
        (RT #93962). Decode before the optional converter, preserve literal
        entity text and add the original workbook as a regression fixture.
      - Resolve built-in number formats and apply row/column default styles
        when a cell has no explicit style (RT #101636). Cell styles override
        row styles, which override column defaults; preserve raw values.
        Add regression tests for decimals, percentages and built-in dates.
      - Resolve absolute and relative worksheet relationship targets and
        normalize dot segments (RT #86667). Report missing targets with sheet
        and relationship details; reject external targets and root traversal.
        Preserve chartsheet placeholders and add regression tests.
      - Replace legacy match and postmatch variables with local captures and
        match lengths (RT #70879), without raising the minimum Perl version.
      - Preserve token boundaries around escaped and quoted literals when
        detecting date formats (RT #87746). Add the original workbook and
        regression tests for date types, raw values and formatted output.
      - Handle line breaks and other XML whitespace in Relationship tags
        (RT #111087). Add regression tests for LF, CRLF and attribute order.
      - Avoid uninitialized-value warnings for undefined shared-string cell
        values during parsing and formatting (RT #114521). Preserve raw undef
        values and add regression tests.
      - Fix short and long weekday formatting and recognize standalone date
        and AM/PM formats as date/time cells (RT #117007). Ignore quoted and
        escaped literals during date-type detection; add regression tests.
      - Support inlineStr cells (RT #117462, #83399), including rich text,
        whitespace, empty strings, converters and separate phonetic metadata.
        Share text extraction with shared strings; add regression tests.
      - Fix AM/PM and A/P time formatting, including uppercase tokens, noon
        and midnight (RT #119170). Preserve raw date/time values and types.
      - Ignore the x15:workbookPr extension instead of rejecting it as a
        prefixed data element. Add the original RT #119170 workbook as a test.
      - Keep phonetic hints out of shared-string cell values (RT #122340).
        Expose hints and their properties separately as RPh and PhoneticPr.
      - Report obvious XML syntax errors and unsupported prefixed elements
        with the XML member name; recommend Spreadsheet::ParseXLSX for prefixed
        files (RT #124409). Document that XML is not fully validated.
      - Include worksheet, XML member and invalid address in cell-reference
        errors. No new XML parser dependency is required.
      - Preserve custom number formats referenced by multiple cell styles
        (RT #132420). Add regression tests for repeated format IDs.
      - Move MaxCol initialization outside the row loop in the SYNOPSIS
        example (RT #140481).
      - Remove unused variables from ValFmt (RT #158167).
      - Fix multiline cell values and value tags with attributes (GitHub PR #1).
        Preserve whitespace and add regression tests.

